{"id": "Dd6P9YOB06z", "title": "Video by nick_saraev", "description": "Comment \"JEV\" to get the setup guide for Laya, the Free and Opensource Jev alternative.\n\nSomeone just released a free and open source version of Jev, and it's actually way faster and cheaper.\n\nIt's called Laya.\n\nIt's a classifier model that you can run locally on your own computer.\n\nIt does the exact same job as Jev.\n\nBut it only takes around 30 milliseconds to answer, while Jev takes around 200.\n\nThe only problem is that the base model isn't good at everything out of the box.\n\nSo it needs to be fine tuned and trained for your specific use case.\n\nAnd you can do that with the help of Claude Code.\n\nOnce done, it can even match Jev on accuracy.\n\nThink of it like getting a raw engine instead of a finished car, it's faster once you tune it, but you have to do that tuning yourself first.\n\nMost people skip this step and end up disappointed with the base model's accuracy.\n\nFine tuning is really where the real performance gap closes.\n\n#jevai #typesafeai #layaai #opensourceai #githubrepo", "channel": "nick_saraev", "uploader_id": "72269881052", "uploader": "Nick Saraev", "timestamp": 1790768407, "like_count": 2663, "comment_count": 2848, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1372048781426494a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 64.679, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.famd5-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQN6OT6o_VoWfP0yD1fTheAA5DNvNVOGB6S9yOc4LuLvx8mLiQmK2XNi3ffeg97iWIYR8CUt_lT5BSDX_2-uge_C9ffPUKFWtqX8Tks.mp4?_nc_cat=100&_nc_oc=AdrgEMm3PEk_0y-BIb2kiphrT5YEdJhBSbU3uDUUaO4LQ4QGf62Q2ctzcc7hKuRC-Xc&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.famd5-1.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=Pu4mRETkevYQ7kNvwFQcJ80&%3D%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=CPl1amnDqPFNtZSo4-oJEg&_nc_ss=70a8c&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQT3liIhw0YD_FbApC6w4e6ziYbvFvaxEMJs3U_jjVUYHg&oe=6AE5F8C5",